## STEP A → D (raised floor — no bare scaffold)

A **scaffold** lesson (frontmatter + stub B1) is not done. Done means CT/CD parity:

1. Map unit to ≥1 CONTENIDOS anchor + competency codes + critical moment.  
2. Run `curriculum-forger` STEP A (UbD, Bloom, CLT) via bridge
   `~/src/.cursor/skills/curriculum-forger/references/institution-nm.md`.  
3. Write `forge/unit-enrichment/U*/MAIN-IDEAS.yml` (≤ 6 ideas; slide sentences
   human; Chicago or `studio_hypothesis`).  
   **Campaign exemplars (binding):** before locking MAIN-IDEAS / Masterclass /
   labs, open
   [`~/src/profield/runs/fashion-exemplary-social-campaigns/CANONICAL.md`](file:///Users/ruvebal/src/profield/runs/fashion-exemplary-social-campaigns/CANONICAL.md)
   → run `20260925T200000Z` **`TEACHING-CAMPAIGN-LEDGER.md`** (ranked) +
   `SUMMARY.md`. Attach **≥1 ranked campaign** per theoretical pod with its
   **canonical URL**. Prefer ranks 1–12 for core pods. Prefer Ahmes rows in
   `VERIFIED-CAMPAIGNS.md` (UNEP Playbook) only when the slide needs a vault
   quote. Contested Zara/BDS cases (`CONTESTED` in the ledger) are seminar
   material — never present as unlabelled “ethical” brand wins. Classify each
   case as Track A (brand/designer), B (Spain–Ibero), or C (movement) — never
   collapse the three.  
4. Resolve Ahmes quotes with `semantic-quote` (never vector snippets).  
   Campaign extracts from the Playbook use the same gate: blockquote + Chicago
   `(United Nations Environment Programme 2023, p.)` + gated
   `curriculum-internal` (`ahmes_coat` · `node_id` · `evaluator_safe`).  
5. Emit full lesson ES under `docs/lessons/es/nuevos-medios-moda/<slug>/`.  
6. **Mandatory media slots** (same law as `dc-unit-forge` §3b): after opener,
   include `lesson-conceptual-graph-slot.html` + `lesson-deck-photo-slot.html`
   with HTML comments for (a) `grounding-graph` → `visual-forger` generative
   request tied to the Master idea, and (b) naturalistic photo prompt for
   Masterclass deck backgrounds. Editorial note must name both slots as
   addressed-to-editor until assets ship. AI links →
   `/ai-declaration/#ai-assisted-authorship`.  
7. **Cold B1** — one Thessia pass per Masterclass idea via `lesson-scribe`
   (`thessia_generate.py`); six-axis cold review → amend → integrate.  
8. B2 = Canvas activity brief; B3 = individual problem/quiz.  
9. Ship Reveal deck at `docs/tracks/es/uem/2627-nm/<slug>/` (cover → analysis →
   ≤6 masterclass → lab opener → 2 labs → outro; geometrical openers from
   `assets/images/fractal-pass-track/`). Slideshow sentences never Thessia.
   Masterclass slides carry a one-line **Caso:** under the human sentence when
   a campaign exemplifies the pod (not a second invented quote). When the
   photographic slot ships, prefer it as Masterclass `background_url` (text
   contrast checked); keep geometrical for lab/workshop openers.  
10. Conceptual graph via `visual-forger` + `grounding-graph` is **required** for
    forge-complete (not optional); U2/U5 may add a second strategy/timeline
    figure.  
11. Register `lessons.yml`; link lesson + deck from track page; write Thessia
    performance receipt under `forge/`.  
12. EN twin: structure + teaching-language notice only.

## Real campaigns as theory pods (always)

Theoretical claims (brainprint, presence system, power map, claims audit…)
must be illustrated with **named, ranked campaigns** from Profield
`fashion-exemplary-social-campaigns` (`TEACHING-CAMPAIGN-LEDGER.md`) — not
generic “una marca X”. Refresh the bank from `CANONICAL.md` on every forge
wave; when the operator adds internet research, merge into that field’s next
pass and re-rank before treating new names as canonical.

## Cite law — lessons only (fail-closed)

**Profield does not need Ahmes.** Profield maps the field (passes, digests,
keywords). It is discovery and routing. Do not block or rewrite Profield runs
to require vault nodes.

**Lessons do.** Every scholarly **quote** and Chicago citation that reaches
student HTML must resolve to an Ahmes node you opened (`semantic-quote` /
`ahmes query --cite` with `evaluator_safe=yes`), or stay `[BIBLIO-GAP]` /
`OMITTED`. Never cite vector snippets as quotes.

| Layer | Ahmes required? |
| --- | --- |
| Profield FieldSpec / pass1–3 / digest | **No** |
| Lesson blockquotes + References + `PROVENANCE_LINE` | **Yes** |
| Thessia cold B1 prose cadence | Quotes locked **before** Thessia; strip any cite/quote Thessia invents |

If Thessia invents a quote, DOI, page, or author: **strip it**. Do not
“normalize” a fake into a plausible extract. Prefer fewer quotes to invented ones.

See [`forge/PROVENANCE-LAW.mdc`](./forge/PROVENANCE-LAW.mdc) and
[`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md).

